<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20426] add per-operation lnet latency stats</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20426</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;LNet exposed no per-operation latency, only send, receive and drop counts and credit levels in "lnetctl peer show -v". When a cluster performance problem was suspected to be in the network there was no per-peer or per-NI latency to confirm or refute it, and rebuilding it from +net debug timestamps is impractical under concurrent load. LNet should track latency and expose these stats through lnetctl.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
